 shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${A}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}}\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186115851 "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations $R_{1}:=R_{1} + (-1)R_{2}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-2)R_{1}$?\n\n$$\nA = \\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}5 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{array} \\right] , \\hspace{2em} B = \\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}- 2 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 1\\end{array} \\right] , \\hspace{2em} C = \\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{array} \\right]\n$$"] [17592186115853 "The inverse of the matrix $A$ is found using the row operations as shown below. What are the corresponding row operations?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186115884 "Let $A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ -3 & k\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne -1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [17592186235397 "The solution of the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+1 &=0 \\\\ 4x+3y-3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n