n below. Complete the process, and determine ${P}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}{}[P\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}I] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}-3 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{5}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{3}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}}\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}$$"] [17592186573266 "The inverse of the matrix $B$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[B\\,|\\,I] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186573325 "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $H$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${H}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}{}[H\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}I] & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}}\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}$$"] [17592186605111 "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3y &=4 \\\\ 2x+y &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$\\mathbf{x}=$</span>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">{{field-1}}</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$1$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$4$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-5$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186605144 "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x &=3 \\\\ 2x-5y &=-11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$\\mathbf{x}=$</span>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">{{field-1}}</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-2$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$3$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-11$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186607568 "The solution of the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+1 &=0 \\\\ 17x-28y-15 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ngives the point where the paths meet. This solution can be written in matrix form as\n\n$$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{67}\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{a} & \\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{b} \\\\ -17 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ \\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{c}\\end{bmatrix}$$\n\nFind the values of $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,c\\,=$\n{{field-3}}"] [17592186613762 "The solution of the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-5 &=0 \\\\ 5x+3y-10 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ngives the point where the dirt tracks meet. This solution can be written in matrix form as\n\n$$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{a} & \\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{b} \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ \\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{c}\\end{bmatrix}$$\n\nFind the values of $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,c\\,=$\n{{field-3}}"] [17592186642299 "Let \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\det(A)=1$\n\nII. ${A}^{-1}$ does **not** exist\n\nIII. $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $\\mathbf{b}$"] [17592186642304 "Consider a system of two linear equations in two variables, represented by the matrix equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ in the usual way. Given that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\det(A)=0$\n\nIII. $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has a unique solution (the trivial solution)"]}
